{"chunk_id": "b1a64c94d57d", "text": "Saunaka asks what the mighty serpents did after hearing their mother\u2019s curse. Sauti narrates the story of Sesha, the noblest among them. Disturbed by the cruelty, jealousy, and hostility of his brothers\u2014especially toward Vinata and her son Garuda\u2014Sesha abandons them and undertakes severe ascetic penance across sacred regions such as Gandhamadana and the Himalaya. His austerities become so intense that Brahma appears and asks his purpose. Sesha declares he wishes to avoid the company of his wicked kin and devote himself to virtue. Pleased by this restraint, Brahma grants him a cosmic duty: to support the unstable Earth. Sesha agrees, descending beneath the world and bearing it upon his head. Thus he becomes Ananta, the eternal serpent whose steadfast virtue literally upholds the world.\nSesha performs severe penance, rejects his wicked serpent brothers, and is tasked by Brahma to support the Earth beneath the world.\nThemes: asceticism, cosmic duty, family discord, divine boon, world-supporting serpent", "vector": [0.017483357340097427, -0.01340798195451498, -0.00368142151273787, 0.004720642231404781, -0.0014510031323879957, 0.017306756228208542, -0.03415163978934288, -0.009740144945681095, -0.0072066206485033035, -0.01317704375833273, 0.009699391201138496, 0.012783091515302658, 0.029940417036414146, 0.012457061558961868, 0.01213782373815775, -0.01566302217543125, 0.04257407784461975, -0.002513147657737136, 0.02211569808423519, 0.0033944472670555115, -0.0018067493801936507, -0.009488830342888832, 0.003399541601538658, 0.01960255205631256, -0.018760306760668755, 0.0054677939042449, 0.025090722367167473, -0.02890799008309841, -0.009026954881846905, -0.011900093406438828, 0.0034912375267595053, -0.0012667622650042176, -0.005926273763179779, 0.006442487705498934, -0.02934269607067108, 0.0017558071995154023, -0.010758988559246063, -0.01509246975183487, 0.006802479270845652, -0.021191947162151337, -0.001959575805813074, 